course: dictionary
lesson: 15975
title: Unzip
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To unzip something means to open its zip, so the teeth come apart and the thing can open. «Mia unzipped her coat because the classroom was hot.» The coat was closed with a zip, and she pulled it open.
explain: The word starts with un-. Un- often means "the opposite of" or "undo", so unzip is the opposite of zip. Zip means to close something with a zip, and unzip goes back the other way.
explain: Computers use the word too. A file can be squashed small and zipped, like a packed suitcase. «Sam unzipped the folder to find his homework.» To unzip a file means to open it so you can use what is inside.
fact: Unzip is a verb. Its other forms are unzips, unzipped and unzipping.
fact: «Unzip» means to open the zip on a coat, bag, tent or pencil case.
fact: «Unzip» can also mean to open a zipped file on a computer so you can use what is inside.
fact: The prefix un- often means "the opposite of" or "undo", as in unlock, untie and unzip.
exercise: «Mia unzipped her coat because the classroom was hot.» What did Mia do to her coat? | *Opened its zip | Washed it | Closed its zip | Lost it
exercise: «Sam unzipped the folder to find his homework.» On a computer, what did Sam do? | *Opened a zipped file to use what is inside | Sent the folder to the bin | Deleted his homework | Shut the computer down
exercise: What does the un- at the start of unzip often mean? | *The opposite of, or undo | Under the ground | Very big | Again and again
test: «Tom had to unzip the tent door to get out.» What action is this? | Painting the door | *Opening the zip | Folding the tent away | Sewing a hole in the tent
test: «Ruby zipped her pencil case shut, then unzipped it to find a rubber.» What did Ruby do first, then second? | Opened it, then zipped it shut | *Zipped it shut, then opened it | Lost it, then found it | Painted it, then dried it
exam: Which sentence uses unzip correctly? | *«I unzipped my bag to get my reading book.» | «The rain unzipped the river.» | «The bird unzipped the sky at noon.» | «I unzipped the sun to make it hot.»
